/* book exam traps: Dividing the wrong way: actual trays = theoretical / Eo. An efficiency below one must increase the count, never decrease it. | yn* is equilibrium with the liquid leaving tray n, not with the liquid entering the tray. Using the incoming liquid gives a false driving force. | Eo and EM are not interchangeable. Eo counts whole-column trays; EM is a local vapour ratio on one tray. | HETP has units of length. Multiplying Nt by HETP gives packed height in metres, not a number of trays. | Weeping, flooding and entrainment are hydraulic limits, not efficiency values. A high EM does not excuse a column that floods. | Dividing a stage count that includes the reboiler by Eo. The reboiler is one ideal stage already; take it off first. */
