/* book: lead: Multicomponent distillation separates three or more volatile components, and binary McCabe-Thiele no longer fits because every component distributes between the products. Shortcut methods give a fast first design: pick two key components, then Fenske for the minimum stages, Underwood for the minimum reflux and Gilliland for the stages at the chosen reflux. */
/* book Figure 4.8.1: The Gilliland correlation in its Molokanov form, with the two columns of this unit marked: the ternary benzene-toluene-xylene example (X = 0.143 gives Y = 0.512 and N = 18.4) and the binary McCabe-Thiele column at R = 2, where the correlation gives 13.1 stages against 13 from the staircase. */
