/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An azeotrope is a composition at which the vapour and liquid in equilibrium have the same mole fractions: yi = xi.
   - yi and xi are mole fractions of i in vapour and liquid; αij is the relative volatility of i to j.
   - Azeotropic distillation adds an entrainer, a third component that forms a new, lower-boiling azeotrope with one of the feed components.
   - Extractive distillation feeds a high-boiling, relatively nonvolatile solvent near the top of the column.
   - Pressure-swing distillation uses two columns at different pressures.
*/
