/* book exam traps: Believing a taller column can cross an azeotrope. At α = 1 every stage leaves the composition unchanged; the equilibrium curve meets the diagonal there. | Saying the entrainer and the extractive solvent both leave at the bottom. The entrainer leaves overhead in its new azeotrope; the extractive solvent leaves at the bottom and is recycled. | Taking the azeotrope composition as fixed at every pressure. It shifts with pressure, which is what pressure-swing distillation uses. | Treating 95.6 mass % ethanol as 95.6 mol %. With molar masses 46.07 and 18.02 kg/kmol the azeotrope is about 89.5 mol % ethanol. | Assuming any added liquid breaks the azeotrope. The agent must change the relative volatility strongly and be recoverable at low cost. */
